@@ -8,24 +8,40 @@ npm start        # http://localhost:3000, data in tasks.db (PORT and DB_PATH cha
 npm test         # the API tests (node:test)
 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "status": "todo", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+
+`status` is `"todo"` (the default), `"doing"` or `"done"`. `done` is deprecated: see [Deprecated](#deprecated).
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?status=todo\|doing\|done` keeps the tasks in that status; `?done=true\|false` (deprecated) keeps the done ones or the others (`todo` and `doing`) | 200, an array of tasks, or 400 for an unknown `status` |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "status": "todo" }` (`status` optional, `todo` by default) | 201, the task, or 400 for an invalid `status` |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `status` (`done` is deprecated) | 200, the task, 400 for an invalid `status`, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
-Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
+Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`. A `status` that is not `todo`, `doing` or `done` (an unknown string, a
+non-string, `null` or an empty string), in a body or in `?status=`, answers 400 `{ "error": "status must be todo, doing or done" }`
+and changes nothing.
+
+## Deprecated
+
+`status` replaces `done`. `done` is kept for one release and **will be removed next release**:
+
+- responses still carry `done`, `true` exactly when `status` is `"done"`;
+- `PATCH` still accepts `done: true` (sets `status` to `done`) and `done: false` (sets `status` to `todo`);
+- `GET /api/tasks?done=true` lists the `done` tasks and `?done=false` the `todo` and `doing` ones;
+- `POST` does not read `done`.
+
+When `status` and `done` are both sent (in a `PATCH` body or in the query), `status` wins and `done` is ignored.
+Existing databases are migrated on startup (migration 2): `done = 1` becomes `status = 'done'`, `done = 0` becomes `'todo'`.
 
 ## Layout
 
-- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
+- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied; migration 2 replaced `done` with `status`).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
 - `public/`: the page.
-- `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
+- `test/`: the API tests and the migration test, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
